CAPTURE REPORT - FOUR-TAILS HOST (ROSHI)
Status: COMPLETE. Beast sealed.

Target: Roshi of the Hidden Rock, jinchuriki of the Four-Tails, Son Goku. A Lava
Release user who had long since left his village and wandered alone - an ideal
acquisition, isolated and unguarded by any Kage.

Engagement: the assigned cell tracked the target through Zetsu's reconnaissance and
subdued him away from populated ground. His Lava Release and partial beast
transformation were accounted for in the approach; containment held.

Delivery: host transported alive to the Gedo Statue chamber. Full ten-ring extraction
conducted over three days. Son Goku sealed; the Statue's fourth eye now open.

Assessment: model operation. Hosts who abandon their villages are the softest targets
we have. Prioritise the remaining unaffiliated jinchuriki on the same principle.
